 "equipment_type": "Pump controller (fire-fighting booster switch box)",
 "applies_to": "Wilo SCe switch boxes on fire-fighting (FFS) booster sets in the Polish variant.",
 "summary": "Wilo's SC-family switch boxes control multi-pump systems and act as a BACnet MS/TP slave on their RS-485 port; BACnet IP needs an added gateway in the panel. The SCe FFS Poland list covers the operating command, setpoints, pump modes, pump state bits, running hours and error bits. Fieldbus write access is governed by a bus command timer that must be refreshed every five minutes.",
 "bacnet_transport": [
  "BACnet MS/TP",
  "BACnet IP"
 ],
 "firmware": "Data-point list 31.200",
 "default_device_instance": null,
 "access_inferred": false,
 "notes": [
  "Taken from the 'SCe FFS Poland' table in Wilo's SC BACnet supplement (English part, pp89-91). Wilo prints a 'BACnet ID' and an object type with its BACnet type code in brackets, e.g. 'Analog Input (0)'. The ID is used here as the instance and the type follows the code, so rows printed 'Binary Input (4)' are Binary Outputs.",
  "Where Wilo prints several IDs against one name (pump state, switch box state, error state and other bitmaps), each ID is its own binary object for the element printed beside it; the element is shown in brackets after the name.",
  "Analog objects that list several units report in the unit of the active control mode."
 ],
 "integration": {
  "summary": "Map Drives on/off (BO 224) as the start/stop command and Set point 1 (AO 1072) as the setpoint. For fieldbus control, write Set to the Bus command timer (MO 208) and repeat it within five minutes. Read the collective run and fault signals (BI 976/977) and the Error state bits for alarms; acknowledge with BO 1985.",
  "minimum_points": [
   {
    "ref": "BO 224",
    "name": "Drives on/off",
    "why": "Automatic operation and all pumps on/off"
   },
   {
    "ref": "AO 1072",
    "name": "Set point 1",
    "why": "Setpoint 1; unit follows the control mode"
   },
   {
    "ref": "MO 208",
    "name": "Bus command timer",
    "why": "Write Set (3) at least every 5 min to keep control"
   },
   {
    "ref": "BO 1985",
    "name": "Acknowledge",
    "why": "Alarm acknowledge"
   },
   {
    "ref": "BI 976",
    "name": "Switch box state (SBM)",
    "why": "Collective run signal"
   },
   {
    "ref": "AI 400",
    "name": "Current value",
    "why": "Measured value; unit follows the control mode"
   },
   {
    "ref": "BI 977",
    "name": "Switch box state (SSM)",
    "why": "Collective fault signal"
   }
  ],
  "enable": "The Bus command timer (MO 208) decides who may change settings. Manual: HMI and fieldbus both write, last value wins. Off: HMI locked, fieldbus only. Set: HMI locked and a 5-minute timer starts (state reads Active).",
  "heartbeat": "With the Bus command timer in Set mode, Set must be written again at least every five minutes. If it lapses the state changes to Reset, the HMI gets access back and the fieldbus is locked until Set is written again.",
  "remote_sensors": null,
  "setup": [
   "SC menus 5.1.2.1-5.1.2.5 set the BACnet MS/TP baud rate, bus address (MAC), parity, stop bits and device object ID.",
   "BACnet IP uses an extra gateway (HD67686) wired to the panel's RS-485 port: set the SC to 38400 baud, MAC 5, no parity, 1 stop bit. The gateway defaults to 192.168.0.10, UDP 47808, no DHCP; change it with the free Compositor SW67686 tool.",
   "Terminate the first and last node of the MS/TP segment (DIP switch or jumper, per panel hardware)."
  ],
  "gotchas": [
   "In Bus command timer Off mode the HMI stays locked; if the fieldbus fails there is no access until it recovers.",
   "Alarm history: write the index (0-15 on SC) to AO 1990, then read the error code from AI 1995.",
   "Active setpoint value (AO 416) is read-only on SCe NWB boxes."
  ]
 },
